# Branch Name Format

Keep the branch name short and human-readable. The linked GitHub issue number is already carried, canonically, by the **commit subject** (`commit-message-one-line.mdc`) and the **PR title** (`pr-title-format.mdc`). Repeating it in the branch name is noise — branches get renamed, abandoned, and relanded, while issue→commit→PR is the stable thread.

## Rule

```
<owner>/<short-kebab-slug>
```

- `<owner>` is your GitHub login (or the team prefix the repo already uses).
- `<short-kebab-slug>` is 2–6 lowercase hyphen-separated words in imperative voice, describing the change. Aim for ≤ 50 characters total including the owner.

## Good vs bad

```
✅ mouliraj/document-trace-warmup
✅ tivince82/reshape-l1-small-opt-in
✅ friedrich/tilize-block-factory-l1-budget
✅ mouliraj/reject-int-float-datacopy

❌ mouliraj/61727-document-trace-warmup-and-fail-on-unsafe-alloc (issue number duplicated; already in commit + PR title)
❌ fix-61727-reshape-trace-mapping-collision (missing <owner>/, and issue number embedded)
❌ mouliraj/fix_reshape_trace_bug (underscores — not kebab)
❌ mouliraj/FixReshapeTraceBug (camelCase — not kebab)
❌ mouliraj/really-long-branch-name-that-reads-like-a-sentence-and-describes-everything-about-the-fix (too long; move detail to the commit / PR body)
```

## Why the issue number lives elsewhere

- `pr-title-format.mdc` requires `#<issue-number>: <imperative sentence>` in the PR title.
- `commit-message-one-line.mdc` requires the same `#<issue-number>:` prefix on the commit subject.
- `pipeline-compare.mdc` locates runs by `head_sha`, not by branch name, so putting the issue in the branch doesn't help the audit either.

Issue → commit → PR title → CI run already form the stable key. The branch is just a working-copy label.

## Exception

Throwaway local work that will **never** become a PR may use any prefix:

- `scratch/*`, `wip/*`, `experiment/*`.

If a scratch branch gets promoted to a real PR, rename it to the canonical shape:

```bash
git branch -m <owner>/<short-slug>
git push origin -u <owner>/<short-slug>
# Let the stranded scratch branch expire or delete it on the remote.
```

## Never

- Don't embed the issue number — it's already in the commit subject and PR title.
- Don't use the PR number either (PRs can be superseded by relands).
- Don't use underscores or camelCase — kebab only.
- Don't write a sentence-length slug — if the change needs that much context, the PR description is the place for it.
